SQL LIKE wildcard characters in user input are not escaped. A user searching for `%` or `_` will get unintended results (`%` matches everything, `_` matches any single character). Since the input is passed as a bind parameter, this is a data correctness issue, not a classic injection, but it still allows unexpected query expansion.

Suggestion: escape LIKE metacharacters in the input before constructing the pattern:
```typescript
const escaped = query.trim().replace(/[%_]/g, (ch) => `\${ch}`);
const like = `%${escaped}%`;
```

